            <div xml:id="d50">

                <pb facs="0119" n="59" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg59"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr.
                            Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-14"><hi rendition="#italic">October 14, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Nov. 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 425.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 385, of July 18, 1895,
                    I have the honor to state that I have been informed by the minister for foreign
                    affairs that the two soldiers charged with the killing of the American seamen at
                    Santa Catharina, and who, after being adjudged guilty by the lower court,
                    appealed their case, have been convicted and sentenced to eight years each in
                    the penitentiary.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. L.
                    Thompson</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
